+## Sales and variance
+
+- `POST /import/sales` takes `{ "csv": "..." }` with the columns
+  `ticket,soldAt,dishId,qty` (`soldAt` an ISO instant, `qty` a whole number).
+  Each dish sold uses one portion of its recipe per `qty`; the ingredients
+  are consumed at `soldAt` with ref `sale:<ticket>`. Tickets already
+  imported are skipped. Answers `{ "tickets": n, "dishes": n }` (dishes is
+  the sum of `qty` imported). A bad row is `bad_request` and an item running
+  out is `sale_not_enough_stock`; both name the row (`row 2` is the first
+  data row) and nothing from the file is imported.
+- `GET /reports/variance?from=YYYY-MM-DD&to=YYYY-MM-DD` lists, per item,
+  `theoretical` (use from sales sold in those days), `actual` (every
+  `consume` movement in those days) and `difference` (actual - theoretical),
+  for items where either is above zero.
